-- the construction as a diagnostic, which is what a knowledge graph would actually run. Given a record --
-- a compound's atoms, its bond-graph symmetries, those of them that also preserve the arrangement at every
-- carbon, the counted hydrogens and the peaks its spectrum reports -- there are four cases, and which one
-- a record is in is decidable from the record:
--   0  the three numbers agree: nothing to explain.
--   1  the bond graph's count differs from the configured count and the configured count is the reported
--      peak count: the representation is wrong and the construction is right, which is the case the
--      field's records are in for most compounds with a stereocentre.
--   2  the two counts agree and the peaks are fewer: no representation defect, an accidental coincidence
--      of shift.
--   3  both: the representation is wrong and a coincidence hides part of the difference, which is the case
--      where a validation by peak counts can score the wrong representation as correct.
diagnose : Compd → Nat
diagnose c = case eqb (compd-graph-count c) (compd-conf-count c) of
  true → (case eqb (compd-conf-count c) (compd-peaks c) of true → 0; false → 2)
  false → (case eqb (compd-conf-count c) (compd-peaks c) of true → 1; false → 3)
